{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact c254e207bf12b04713942568fb16486c28d9b60e, complete three-subject C2 revision 5 design. One P2: reconcile the stop/save capacity joins and witness with final adopted R3 revision 18, as governing d33a258e requires.\n\nP2 final-authority alignment: C2 main 1687 (way 2), B1 at 3240 and example 3556–3572 retain proposed R3 revision 17 assumptions. Current example has a RUNNING task, C7 CURRENT and 63 pinned KEPT checkpoints occupying all 64 actual checkpoint places, then a standing-room pause that opens no save. Effective planner adoption 9e1c77cd makes R3 exact 99bc48e8 authoritative: 3666–3669 reserves cancel room from task establishment and pause room from apply/resume RUNNING, including the save closure; 7274–7291 requires the whole remaining three-cut/one-checkpoint closure or already-held places; 7502 states the running full-scope cancel uses standing save room. Used plus reserved places must obey the maxima. That RUNNING/all-64-actual setup cannot coexist with the required standing checkpoint reservation, and B1's one-cut request lowers the adopted closure. This is a bounded design coordination defect, not an observed source pin bypass or executed failure.\n\nRepair the existing way-2/B1/standing table/14.8 joins against the final adopted R3. Preserve whole-closure standing reservations; use a reachable declared newly admitted stop case, or explicitly qualify an invalid reservation history rather than treating it as a valid adopted-rule witness. No new capacity engine, numerical gate, test suite or provider action is needed. Retain B2 save-only admission and B3 host-custody/final-destruction obligations and actual stopped-unsaved paths. Merely recording known dirty-work loss does not fulfill the user's full recovery story.\n\nNonblocking witness clarification for the same repair: 3561–3562 pins all 63 KEPT roots, 3574 releases no pin, yet 3575 expires one KEPT root. The expiry rule 2269–2283 excludes pinned roots